# Missing logos / apparels before naming

Supervisor 2026-09-17: dropping missing logos **after** Step 6 naming leaves process/item gaps. The packing pipeline must strip them **after Step 5, before Step 6**.

Supervisor 2026-10-29: **missing apparels** follow the same gate — detect with the same image dry-run as Preflight / Step 8, exclude the union of missing-logo and missing-apparel rows (and merge siblings), write holding CSVs, then name remaining rows.

Lookup still expands Item Quantity and applies custom `base` / `base-1` stems (same as PDF). Kept Step 5 rows stay unexpanded so Step 6 names remaining rows with no holes. Do not move the filter back after naming.

Holding files (no process/item numbers):

- `Missing Logos/{date}/{shift}/missing_logo_orders_{token}.csv`
- `Missing Apparels/{date}/{shift}/missing_apparel_orders_{token}.csv`

When images exist, run that file through the **main packing app from Step 1** (full pipeline). Fresh names happen on that run.
